WEBVTT

00:07.882 --> 00:10.385
[somber, emotional music]

00:24.649 --> 00:26.276
[whimpering]

00:45.795 --> 00:47.797
[blimp engine rumbling]

01:04.147 --> 01:06.691
Allow me to introduce my game to you.

01:06.775 --> 01:08.401
[wind whistling]

01:08.485 --> 01:11.821
This game,
the one that we're all about to play,

01:11.905 --> 01:13.239
is called… [gasps]

01:13.323 --> 01:15.283
…The Queen of Croquet!

01:16.701 --> 01:17.869
Croquet?

01:19.037 --> 01:20.955
[Mira] Lawn billiards
is what they used to call it

01:21.039 --> 01:24.167
in 19th-century England,
at the height of its popularity.

01:24.667 --> 01:28.296
I don't believe that it was ever
quite so popular in Japan.

01:29.672 --> 01:30.924
We don't know the rules.

01:32.133 --> 01:34.886
[Mira] That's all right.
You don't really need to.

01:35.929 --> 01:36.971
Don't worry.

01:38.223 --> 01:40.683
It doesn't matter which one of us wins!
[laughs]

01:41.434 --> 01:42.310
What?

01:43.686 --> 01:45.897
Clearing Croquet is simple.

01:45.980 --> 01:47.315
You just have to complete

01:47.398 --> 01:50.652
three little sets of croquet games
without withdrawing.

01:51.319 --> 01:54.197
If you decide to give up, game over.

01:54.280 --> 01:56.032
Weapons are also allowed here.

01:56.908 --> 01:58.118
It's so simple.

01:58.993 --> 02:01.329
Just three little rounds of croquet.

02:04.749 --> 02:07.252
W-- We just have to finish three rounds?

02:08.169 --> 02:10.130
We don't even have to win?

02:10.213 --> 02:12.590
[Mira] Exactly! Simple, huh?

02:15.135 --> 02:17.804
Now, why don't we begin?

02:29.566 --> 02:31.568
[theme music]

03:31.502 --> 03:33.463
[wind whistling]

03:33.546 --> 03:35.673
[Mira] Each side has two balls,

03:35.757 --> 03:38.343
one blue and black,
the other red and yellow.

03:38.426 --> 03:42.764
To win, you need to pass your balls
through the six hoops in a certain order,

03:42.847 --> 03:46.601
then hit the final finishing peg
before your opponent does.

04:02.575 --> 04:03.534
[giggles]

04:15.964 --> 04:16.965
Yes!

04:23.972 --> 04:26.975
The first set's mine.
Better luck next time.

04:28.268 --> 04:29.811
[giggles]

04:30.395 --> 04:33.314
We clear the game
by finishing three sets without quitting.

04:34.565 --> 04:35.984
I'm not gonna forfeit.

04:37.402 --> 04:38.820
There are two sets left.

04:40.238 --> 04:41.656
What is she thinking?

04:47.203 --> 04:49.622
All right, round two now.

05:05.763 --> 05:07.140
[sighs]

05:10.893 --> 05:14.480
[Usagi] It looks like she's dragging
the game out, making it last.

05:16.399 --> 05:18.067
I think she's playing with us.

05:18.651 --> 05:20.236
I need to get a move on.

05:21.237 --> 05:23.239
[Usagi breathing shallowly]

05:38.463 --> 05:40.673
[Mira] Oh! This is so much fun!

05:42.300 --> 05:43.259
[hits ball]

05:44.260 --> 05:45.803
Lovely! [gasps]

05:47.013 --> 05:49.098
At this rate, we'll be playing forever.

05:53.478 --> 05:55.063
[labored breathing]

06:05.365 --> 06:06.783
[exhales]

06:09.994 --> 06:11.079
All right!

06:19.212 --> 06:20.380
[chuckles]

06:25.051 --> 06:26.386
[sighs]

06:43.986 --> 06:44.862
I did it!

06:44.946 --> 06:45.822
I won!

06:46.531 --> 06:47.532
[sighs]

06:50.284 --> 06:53.162
It looks like I lost the second set.

06:53.246 --> 06:55.456
[gasps] You are really talented!

06:56.707 --> 06:58.835
Okay, time for round three.

06:58.918 --> 07:00.169
Hmm…

07:00.920 --> 07:02.755
That was just exhausting.

07:03.714 --> 07:05.633
What say we have some tea, hmm?

07:06.467 --> 07:07.468
[Arisu] Tea?

07:16.936 --> 07:19.689
[Arisu] Forget about the tea.
Let's play the game.

07:20.731 --> 07:22.900
[Mira] But teatime is tradition.

07:22.984 --> 07:25.278
It's proper croquet etiquette.

07:25.862 --> 07:28.614
Now, please, help yourselves.

07:41.961 --> 07:43.421
When this game is over,

07:44.338 --> 07:46.048
will we return to our world?

07:47.842 --> 07:50.094
[Mira] You'll find out
at the end of the game.

07:51.554 --> 07:53.264
Don't talk to her, Arisu.

07:54.432 --> 07:56.350
Don't pay any attention to her.

07:56.434 --> 07:57.435
Remember.

07:58.519 --> 08:00.104
We just need to finish.

08:01.022 --> 08:03.107
[Mira] Why do you want to know so badly?

08:07.570 --> 08:08.988
My best friends died.

08:09.697 --> 08:11.449
They never got to learn the truth.

08:13.534 --> 08:16.579
So I need to find out.
I'm doing it for their sake.

08:18.039 --> 08:20.583
- That's why I made it this far.
- You want to know.

08:21.375 --> 08:23.628
But you also want to return

08:23.711 --> 08:25.546
to your world.

08:25.630 --> 08:26.923
Can we return?

08:28.799 --> 08:29.759
[laughs]

08:29.842 --> 08:31.052
Aww…

08:32.178 --> 08:34.388
I'm afraid I can't tell you that.

08:36.057 --> 08:36.933
[Mira chuckles]

08:37.642 --> 08:38.893
For all you know,

08:39.519 --> 08:42.230
this could be the ruins
of your original world.

08:43.481 --> 08:44.774
See, you say that.

08:45.441 --> 08:47.527
But I bet you don't know anything either.

08:48.694 --> 08:49.904
Yes, I do.

08:49.987 --> 08:51.572
[ominous music]

08:55.076 --> 08:56.160
Hmm.

08:57.411 --> 08:59.413
I guess I have no choice. [laughs]

09:01.082 --> 09:02.833
If you want to know so bad,

09:03.960 --> 09:05.628
then I'll tell you everything.

09:07.004 --> 09:09.006
The whole truth about where we are.

09:17.390 --> 09:21.435
However, when I start,
there's no going back.

09:22.228 --> 09:24.897
Remember that you had to know the answer.

09:26.857 --> 09:28.859
You asked for this, Arisu.

09:33.281 --> 09:34.365
[exhales]

09:35.116 --> 09:37.660
Tell me, have you ever thought…

09:37.743 --> 09:40.246
pictured what the future would be like?

09:40.955 --> 09:42.707
- Future?
- [Mira] Yes.

09:43.583 --> 09:46.460
Nanotechnology and renewable energy,

09:46.544 --> 09:51.007
pluripotent cells, virtual reality,
cryogenics, terraforming.

09:52.883 --> 09:55.678
The science and technology from your era

09:55.761 --> 09:58.889
bursts with mountains
of hope and potential.

10:00.766 --> 10:02.977
Perhaps you should be celebrating,

10:03.060 --> 10:06.063
because all of those things
became a reality.

10:06.814 --> 10:11.152
What's more, technology
rapidly advanced and progressed.

10:11.944 --> 10:15.698
Within 30 years, the economies
of developing countries grew,

10:15.781 --> 10:19.827
and the inequality of living standards
was eventually eliminated.

10:19.910 --> 10:24.665
Fifty years later, gene manipulation
extended the human lifespan.

10:26.042 --> 10:27.084
Wait a second.

10:28.753 --> 10:30.046
What are you saying?

10:31.213 --> 10:32.131
[chuckles]

10:32.757 --> 10:33.966
What are you saying?

10:35.301 --> 10:38.137
I am simply providing information.

10:40.056 --> 10:44.185
I'm telling you about
1,000 years of human history.

10:45.686 --> 10:47.563
[scoffs] A thousand years?

10:48.606 --> 10:49.815
In the future?

10:51.484 --> 10:54.779
After humanity
acquired more advanced knowledge,

10:54.862 --> 10:58.616
it persisted in making
new discoveries in every field.

10:59.283 --> 11:01.077
And so, in short,

11:01.160 --> 11:04.914
approximately ten years after
what you believe is the current year,

11:05.790 --> 11:08.042
virtual reality and avatars

11:08.125 --> 11:11.587
begin to take over
all aspects of people's lives.

11:11.671 --> 11:15.591
After 50 years, cures for dementia,
cancer, and many other maladies

11:15.675 --> 11:17.635
become possible through genetics.

11:17.718 --> 11:20.846
After a hundred,
natural disasters are eliminated

11:20.930 --> 11:23.724
thanks to environmental
and weather control technologies.

11:23.808 --> 11:27.520
After 200 years,
the mechanism of the brain is analyzed.

11:27.603 --> 11:30.231
Memories and thoughts can be transplanted.

11:30.314 --> 11:34.110
After 300, humanity
finally conquers natural death

11:34.193 --> 11:36.737
and extends their lifespan to 300 years.

11:36.821 --> 11:41.033
After 400,
due to a perfect understanding of physics,

11:41.117 --> 11:43.953
humanity unlocks all laws of causality.

11:44.036 --> 11:46.288
Coincidence and fate are no more.

11:46.997 --> 11:50.668
After 500,
there are no irregular occurrences.

11:51.168 --> 11:54.505
Humankind is perfectly able
to control its whole world,

11:54.588 --> 11:56.674
basically becoming immortal.

11:56.757 --> 11:58.008
[gasps]

11:58.092 --> 12:01.971
In the 500 years that follow, as long
as they are supplied with dopamine,

12:02.054 --> 12:03.764
humans can live forever.

12:03.848 --> 12:06.016
That's the world in 1,000 years.

12:15.818 --> 12:17.820
[light, ambient music]

12:42.344 --> 12:44.346
[music growing sinister]

12:53.731 --> 12:55.441
[dramatic music]

12:59.820 --> 13:01.822
[rumbling]

13:05.201 --> 13:09.455
[Mira] Right now, you are playing
this game within a virtual reality.

13:10.498 --> 13:13.334
You are so deeply immersed
that you've forgotten.

13:13.417 --> 13:14.960
[energy whirring]

13:15.503 --> 13:19.548
This particular simulation is
the most popular virtual reality package

13:19.632 --> 13:21.509
a thousand years in the future.

13:21.592 --> 13:26.472
After more or less achieving eternal life,
people started losing their drive to live.

13:26.555 --> 13:30.893
And yet, we were enamored with
the period of time a thousand years ago.

13:30.976 --> 13:34.188
A time when people feared death
and the end of the world.

13:34.271 --> 13:36.023
It continued to fascinate us.

13:40.236 --> 13:41.612
Oh, and…

13:41.695 --> 13:44.365
I'm the administrator of this system.

13:51.038 --> 13:52.581
[laughs]

13:52.665 --> 13:53.999
I'm just joking.

13:54.083 --> 13:55.584
Not a word was true.

13:56.418 --> 13:57.837
Huh?

13:57.920 --> 14:00.673
- [Mira giggling]
- Just quit fucking around.

14:00.756 --> 14:01.841
[Mira laughs]

14:03.008 --> 14:04.260
This is the truth.

14:06.345 --> 14:11.058
Genetically modified plants developed
sudden mutations and exploded with growth.

14:12.184 --> 14:13.978
I'm sure you must have noticed.

14:14.687 --> 14:15.729
The city?

14:16.438 --> 14:19.191
It's completely overrun with vegetation.

14:20.985 --> 14:22.069
What's more,

14:23.070 --> 14:25.322
the mountains surround us and close us in.

14:27.575 --> 14:29.076
[somber music]

14:30.619 --> 14:34.081
[Mira] All of that was the work of aliens.

14:36.417 --> 14:37.293
[Arisu] Aliens?

14:38.127 --> 14:41.380
[Mira] They captured all of humanity
and wiped our memories.

14:41.463 --> 14:43.716
Forced us to play countless games.

14:43.799 --> 14:47.011
All so they could conduct
behavioral experiments on us.

14:47.636 --> 14:48.888
[Arisu] Is that…

14:49.680 --> 14:50.806
Is that true?

14:52.766 --> 14:54.393
Of course it is.

14:55.728 --> 14:56.729
Except

14:57.813 --> 15:00.357
a rumor started circulating
among the players.

15:00.983 --> 15:03.402
The ones forced to compete in the games.

15:03.485 --> 15:05.905
A rumor that that wasn't the whole story.

15:05.988 --> 15:08.699
A nuclear apocalypse
had wiped out most life,

15:08.782 --> 15:10.910
and the wealthy elite living underground

15:10.993 --> 15:13.996
had created androids
with artificial memories.

15:14.079 --> 15:17.333
These androids compete in games
on the surface,

15:17.416 --> 15:20.669
and the wealthy place bets
on who would survive.

15:21.921 --> 15:23.923
[emotional music]

15:24.006 --> 15:25.549
[murmur of voices]

15:27.384 --> 15:29.803
[man] A real nail biter,
wouldn't you agree, sir?

15:32.014 --> 15:33.390
Miss? Excuse me.

15:33.474 --> 15:36.435
- Can I place a bet?
- Yes, of course.

15:36.936 --> 15:39.688
[Mira] The players believe
that they are humans,

15:39.772 --> 15:42.942
being forced by aliens
to play these games.

15:43.901 --> 15:45.319
But actually, they…

15:47.029 --> 15:48.197
and you

15:48.280 --> 15:50.866
are simply androids with a collection

15:51.575 --> 15:53.994
of artificial memories.

15:54.078 --> 15:55.371
[crockery rattles]

15:55.454 --> 15:57.122
So is that actually the truth?

15:58.874 --> 16:01.335
[laughs] No! Just kidding.

16:01.418 --> 16:04.171
- [chuckles]
- We need to finish one more set.

16:05.005 --> 16:06.840
Don't listen to what she's saying.

16:07.800 --> 16:10.135
You don't even know
the real answer, do you?

16:13.138 --> 16:14.640
You just might be right.

16:17.685 --> 16:20.020
Do you want the truth so badly?

16:22.439 --> 16:25.651
You want the truth
for the sake of your dead friends?

16:28.821 --> 16:30.364
[gasping]

16:31.907 --> 16:34.284
Oh, you poor, poor thing.

16:35.577 --> 16:37.788
It's written all over your face.

16:38.831 --> 16:42.209
They were tremendously important to you,
weren't they?

16:47.798 --> 16:49.174
You should know,

16:49.258 --> 16:52.428
I'm the one who made that game for you.

16:53.429 --> 16:56.932
I designed the Seven of Hearts
because you three were so close.

16:59.727 --> 17:00.853
Arisu!

17:00.936 --> 17:02.730
- It's all right.
- [Arisu panting]

17:02.813 --> 17:04.440
Please don't stop him.

17:05.357 --> 17:06.775
Let him hate.

17:07.276 --> 17:09.945
Hate is the most incredible motivator.

17:10.612 --> 17:12.614
[tense, punchy music]

17:35.012 --> 17:37.097
It's all part of your plan, isn't it?

17:43.437 --> 17:44.855
You want to get killed.

17:45.731 --> 17:47.566
I'm supposed to shoot you now.

17:49.318 --> 17:50.861
If I kill you in this game,

17:52.112 --> 17:53.447
we won't win.

17:53.530 --> 17:54.948
We won't clear it.

17:55.032 --> 17:56.784
There won't even be a game over.

17:57.743 --> 17:58.744
That means

17:59.620 --> 18:01.997
I would make this game go on forever.

18:03.457 --> 18:04.500
If that happens,

18:05.793 --> 18:09.296
all the other players are doomed
to wait until their visas expire.

18:12.216 --> 18:13.383
You want that.

18:14.551 --> 18:16.512
You want us to fall into despair.

18:17.554 --> 18:19.181
You want us to lose all hope.

18:26.939 --> 18:28.273
[Mira] Tell me something.

18:29.024 --> 18:30.943
While you were playing the games,

18:32.027 --> 18:34.988
did you really care
about the rest of the world?

18:36.448 --> 18:40.160
Were you thinking about how
the world works or what its purpose is?

18:40.953 --> 18:42.329
Your own goals?

18:43.163 --> 18:45.040
Or did you lose interest? Huh?

18:45.833 --> 18:48.293
Did you start to accept
that it didn't matter?

18:48.961 --> 18:49.837
[gasps]

18:51.421 --> 18:53.090
The answer doesn't matter.

18:54.216 --> 18:55.968
And I think you know that.

18:57.344 --> 19:00.514
Arisu. Don't listen to her.

19:00.597 --> 19:02.349
- [Arisu] I wanna know the answer.
- Arisu!

19:02.432 --> 19:03.851
Are you really sure?

19:07.146 --> 19:08.021
Yeah.

19:14.027 --> 19:17.281
It seems like you're prepared
to accept reality.

19:23.370 --> 19:24.580
So be it, then.

19:25.956 --> 19:29.459
I'll stop dodging your questions
and tell you what you want to know.

19:32.212 --> 19:33.672
Let's start with the big one.

19:34.756 --> 19:37.968
The world,
this world in front of your face,

19:38.552 --> 19:39.887
none of it is real.

19:40.804 --> 19:41.889
It's an illusion.

19:44.308 --> 19:45.392
[gasps]

19:46.852 --> 19:49.104
You want me to believe
all of this is a trick?

19:49.688 --> 19:53.483
Arisu, were you never once suspicious
since you arrived?

19:54.109 --> 19:57.404
The desolate city,
and the science far too advanced?

19:57.487 --> 19:58.947
The mysterious games?

19:59.031 --> 20:00.574
Is it humans, or aliens?

20:00.657 --> 20:02.659
That doesn't make any sense, does it?

20:02.743 --> 20:06.538
Even if they were behind all this,
why would they choose to run these games?

20:09.291 --> 20:11.210
Tag, hide-and-seek,

20:11.793 --> 20:13.545
they're children's games.

20:14.046 --> 20:17.633
Nothing beyond your imagination
is possible here.

20:17.758 --> 20:19.343
[soft, ominous music]

20:25.933 --> 20:28.393
It is no surprise that you were right.

20:28.477 --> 20:31.063
You were always meant
to survive this long.

20:33.023 --> 20:34.483
It's simple, really.

20:36.443 --> 20:38.946
This is all taking place in your mind.

20:39.571 --> 20:41.657
This is all in your head, you see.

20:41.740 --> 20:45.327
[chuckles] In a brain
that barely weighs 1,500 grams.

21:02.928 --> 21:03.929
[Usagi] Arisu.

21:04.554 --> 21:06.098
Don't listen to her.

21:07.307 --> 21:08.809
If this were an illusion,

21:09.518 --> 21:11.353
that means I'm not real.

21:11.436 --> 21:15.232
I can't just be something you invented!
Listen, I'm alive and I'm here!

21:15.315 --> 21:17.234
- Of course you are.
- [gasping]

21:18.318 --> 21:20.821
You exist, all right. Of course you do.

21:21.655 --> 21:23.490
But you're somewhere else.

21:23.573 --> 21:27.035
That is not the reality
Arisu is looking at right now.

21:27.619 --> 21:28.704
Huh?

21:30.622 --> 21:31.623
Arisu.

21:33.792 --> 21:35.711
What happened in that moment?

21:36.795 --> 21:38.338
You remember, don't you?

21:42.301 --> 21:43.719
When you lost them.

21:45.512 --> 21:47.848
Those friends
that were so precious to you.

21:49.641 --> 21:50.851
The shock of it

21:51.685 --> 21:53.520
wiped your memories.

21:57.983 --> 21:59.276
I'm your doctor.

22:00.694 --> 22:02.446
My name is Mira Kano.

22:03.071 --> 22:04.072
Remember me?

22:04.990 --> 22:06.283
Your psychiatrist.

22:07.993 --> 22:09.244
I'm helping you.

22:09.870 --> 22:11.955
We are doing therapy together.

22:15.042 --> 22:16.293
You just

22:17.753 --> 22:19.296
don't remember.

22:21.548 --> 22:23.258
You don't remember anything.

22:29.806 --> 22:30.849
So?

22:33.268 --> 22:34.561
What about now?

22:36.897 --> 22:38.231
Your memories…

22:40.525 --> 22:41.985
Are they coming back?

22:44.488 --> 22:45.489
[thump]

22:52.829 --> 22:54.289
[low rumbling]

23:01.463 --> 23:03.465
[ominous, ambient music]

23:27.239 --> 23:29.241
[distant voices echoing]

23:34.746 --> 23:36.665
Arisu, how are you?

23:39.626 --> 23:41.711
Tell me about your memories.

23:41.795 --> 23:43.255
Are they coming back to you?

23:48.552 --> 23:50.345
Chota. [gasps]

23:51.596 --> 23:52.681
Karube.

23:53.932 --> 23:55.308
[sighs]

24:00.147 --> 24:01.189
[sighs]

24:03.733 --> 24:05.944
You're both two peas in a pod.

24:07.529 --> 24:09.114
She's always checking in.

24:10.782 --> 24:13.243
She really worries about you.

24:17.122 --> 24:20.500
She also lost
someone very precious to her.

24:21.668 --> 24:24.588
So she's been hospitalized here.
Just like you.

24:29.217 --> 24:31.011
[gentle music]

24:31.094 --> 24:32.053
[Mira] Now,

24:32.929 --> 24:33.930
tell me.

24:37.601 --> 24:39.811
Tell me what happened to you, Arisu.

24:41.271 --> 24:44.316
On that day with the fireworks.

24:51.031 --> 24:51.948
Go on.

24:53.366 --> 24:54.576
Try to remember.

24:59.623 --> 25:00.916
Fireworks…

25:00.999 --> 25:03.001
- [horn blares]
- [engine revs]

25:03.793 --> 25:05.545
- Whoa! Get off!
- [laughing] Put me down.

25:05.629 --> 25:07.130
- Quick!
- [biker] You guys are crazy!

25:07.214 --> 25:08.757
- [horn blares]
- [all gasping]

25:10.675 --> 25:12.469
- [biker] Watch out! Watch out!
- [horn beeping]

25:12.552 --> 25:14.304
- Hurry up! Come on!
- Aah! Uh, uh--

25:14.387 --> 25:15.555
Look! Fireworks!

25:15.639 --> 25:17.682
- [Arisu] Okay.
- [Karube] Run for your lives!

25:17.766 --> 25:18.934
- [horn blares]
- [tires screech]

25:19.768 --> 25:21.770
[crowd gasp and scream]

25:21.853 --> 25:23.855
[Arisu] Huh? Huh? Huh?

25:24.689 --> 25:26.358
Huh? Huh…

25:31.071 --> 25:32.697
[trembling]

25:35.200 --> 25:36.618
[choral music]

25:45.919 --> 25:47.420
[sobbing quietly]

25:53.301 --> 25:54.844
It was my fault.

25:56.888 --> 25:58.056
And now they're dead.

25:59.849 --> 26:01.685
It seems like you remember now.

26:03.812 --> 26:05.063
[sniffles]

26:07.065 --> 26:08.692
I'm the one who killed them.

26:10.068 --> 26:11.111
My fault…

26:12.862 --> 26:14.823
The answer you're trying to find,

26:16.157 --> 26:17.951
it's not about this world.

26:19.077 --> 26:20.495
Why it exists.

26:22.038 --> 26:24.583
The answer you're really searching for

26:26.418 --> 26:28.420
is what you are.

26:29.754 --> 26:32.215
You want to know why you're alive.

26:33.883 --> 26:35.385
Why you lived.

26:36.261 --> 26:38.305
You want to know why you exist.

26:41.850 --> 26:44.436
You grew up starved for love.

26:46.354 --> 26:48.773
You've been seeking that answer
a long time.

26:50.942 --> 26:52.986
Long before you came here.

26:57.032 --> 26:58.366
So what did you do?

26:59.951 --> 27:01.870
You manifested these games

27:02.579 --> 27:03.872
in your fantasies,

27:04.414 --> 27:07.083
these childlike games
you made for yourself.

27:15.342 --> 27:17.677
And as you kept surviving the games,

27:18.345 --> 27:19.596
you developed the desire

27:19.679 --> 27:22.265
to know the truth about this place.

27:24.601 --> 27:28.063
And that overlapped with your search
for meaning in your own life.

27:29.064 --> 27:31.066
They became intertwined in your head.

27:33.943 --> 27:34.986
[sniffles]

27:35.695 --> 27:36.988
[Mira] Tell me, Arisu…

27:38.948 --> 27:40.825
in this whole world,

27:41.826 --> 27:43.578
is there anyone who needs you?

27:43.662 --> 27:44.579
[sniffles]

27:47.248 --> 27:48.833
[Arisu] I'm not sure I'm ready.

27:49.876 --> 27:52.087
Don't be silly.
You've prepared, haven't you?

27:52.170 --> 27:53.421
- [Arisu] I have, but I--
- Mm-hmm.

27:53.505 --> 27:56.007
[Arisu] I just…
I don't know how much… [voice fading]

27:57.634 --> 28:00.929
[Mira] Is there a reason
you exist in this world?

28:01.012 --> 28:03.181
[dad] I've never had any concerns
about you, son.

28:03.264 --> 28:05.475
[Mira] Does your life have any meaning?

28:05.558 --> 28:07.560
[gunfire in game]

28:10.313 --> 28:12.315
[choral music swells]

28:19.614 --> 28:21.700
What's your life's purpose, son?

28:27.831 --> 28:30.375
How long are you going
to pass your days like this?

28:35.880 --> 28:36.756
Hey.

28:39.175 --> 28:40.927
Is there a reason you're alive?

28:42.262 --> 28:43.680
[game sounds stop]

28:44.347 --> 28:45.557
[Mira] And now

28:46.433 --> 28:48.393
you're the one who survived.

28:55.734 --> 28:56.985
I don't know why.

28:58.862 --> 29:00.697
There's no reason for me to live.

29:05.243 --> 29:06.536
They're the ones

29:07.912 --> 29:09.622
who should have survived.

29:13.835 --> 29:14.836
Karube.

29:16.546 --> 29:17.672
Chota.

29:21.968 --> 29:23.011
Instead, it's me.

29:25.013 --> 29:27.599
I survived. The one with no reason to.

29:35.565 --> 29:37.442
I shouldn't be alive at all.

29:45.784 --> 29:46.868
Arisu.

29:47.368 --> 29:49.454
You need to wait outside for your turn.

29:50.455 --> 29:51.790
We'll be seeing you soon.

29:52.373 --> 29:53.792
[Usagi gasping]

29:53.875 --> 29:55.794
- Arisu!
- [Mira] Leave him alone.

29:56.753 --> 30:00.006
He is trying to remember everything
right now.

30:00.840 --> 30:03.927
[gasping] Hey, hey! Wake up!

30:04.010 --> 30:05.678
- Hey!
- I said stop that!

30:08.640 --> 30:12.977
Arisu's remembering his past
so that he can recover.

30:13.520 --> 30:15.605
And you're interfering with that.

30:16.439 --> 30:18.525
- [gasping] No!
- Step back.

30:23.321 --> 30:24.405
Now,

30:25.698 --> 30:26.825
Arisu…

30:30.203 --> 30:31.871
why don't we make this go away?

30:34.123 --> 30:37.252
All you need to do
is tell me that you're giving up…

30:40.088 --> 30:41.631
and the game will end.

30:42.465 --> 30:44.467
[ominous music]

30:45.301 --> 30:47.720
The game will… end.

30:54.686 --> 30:56.229
That means it's real.

30:57.272 --> 30:59.107
It wasn't an illusion.

31:06.948 --> 31:09.450
I was a player in that game too.

31:11.452 --> 31:12.912
[breathing shakily]

31:22.881 --> 31:23.798
[gasps]

31:23.882 --> 31:25.049
[chuckles]

31:26.593 --> 31:27.927
[cries out]

31:31.097 --> 31:31.973
Now,

31:32.891 --> 31:33.850
Arisu.

31:37.312 --> 31:39.689
Let me be absolutely certain.

31:42.066 --> 31:43.318
You're forfeiting?

31:45.278 --> 31:47.155
You're quitting the game, right?

31:49.240 --> 31:50.909
[breathing unsteadily]

32:09.594 --> 32:12.180
You'll feel better
after you take your medicine.

32:15.099 --> 32:16.100
Go on.

32:17.810 --> 32:19.020
[gasps]

32:24.025 --> 32:25.151
After that,

32:26.694 --> 32:27.862
you can answer.

32:46.923 --> 32:48.716
Arisu, stop it.

32:51.094 --> 32:53.513
Arisu, no!

33:02.271 --> 33:03.690
[Usagi gasps]

33:05.775 --> 33:07.360
[panting]

33:09.237 --> 33:10.780
I would put that down.

33:11.447 --> 33:12.740
[Usagi breathing heavily]

33:17.203 --> 33:18.496
[Usagi whispers] Arisu…

33:23.001 --> 33:24.669
you promised.

33:26.004 --> 33:29.507
You promised you'd protect me,
no matter what.

33:31.009 --> 33:32.719
[Usagi trembling]

33:34.345 --> 33:35.847
Don't listen to her.

33:37.181 --> 33:39.308
I am definitely here with you.

33:41.769 --> 33:42.937
I'm alive!

33:47.817 --> 33:50.278
But if you believe what she says…

33:54.866 --> 33:57.076
then our time together wasn't real.

33:58.828 --> 34:00.121
[sobbing]

34:00.204 --> 34:02.790
It was just something
you created in your mind.

34:08.212 --> 34:10.339
And if you made it all up, then…

34:14.218 --> 34:16.721
then that means I don't matter to you.

34:16.804 --> 34:18.222
[sobs]

34:18.306 --> 34:20.058
And what I do shouldn't affect you.

34:25.271 --> 34:26.522
- [gasps]
- [blood pouring]

34:27.648 --> 34:29.650
[breathing heavily] Arisu!

34:31.235 --> 34:32.487
Wake up.

34:32.570 --> 34:34.322
[whimpering]

34:35.823 --> 34:37.533
[blood dripping]

34:39.035 --> 34:40.661
[sounds fade]

34:47.418 --> 34:49.420
[disconcerting music]

35:04.102 --> 35:06.104
[metronome ticking]

35:08.856 --> 35:10.858
[ominous music]

35:18.324 --> 35:20.326
[ticking continues]

35:29.252 --> 35:31.254
[ticking continues]

35:37.677 --> 35:39.178
[ticking slows]

35:44.684 --> 35:46.394
[ticking regains rhythm]

35:51.983 --> 35:53.985
[ominous music intensifies]

36:05.580 --> 36:07.415
[ticking stops]

36:10.084 --> 36:11.294
[Usagi gasping softly]

36:15.256 --> 36:16.632
[whimpering]

36:20.386 --> 36:21.679
Arisu.

36:31.355 --> 36:32.481
[whispers] Arisu.

36:34.150 --> 36:35.651
You have to come back.

36:37.695 --> 36:39.822
[whimpering] Please.

36:41.991 --> 36:43.201
[sobbing]

36:45.912 --> 36:48.664
What a truly touching display.

36:49.874 --> 36:51.042
However,

36:52.585 --> 36:55.796
the feeling you call love is powerless.

36:55.880 --> 36:57.882
[blood dripping]

37:01.886 --> 37:03.012
Arisu.

37:06.432 --> 37:07.266
Please.

37:09.685 --> 37:10.811
I shouldn't be here.

37:12.438 --> 37:13.898
I shouldn't be alive.

37:15.650 --> 37:17.652
I have no reason to live.

37:20.696 --> 37:22.281
[gasps]

37:30.039 --> 37:31.332
[Usagi] Come back…

37:34.543 --> 37:35.920
Arisu.

37:36.003 --> 37:37.004
[sobs]

37:43.678 --> 37:45.096
[gasping]

37:46.931 --> 37:49.475
[echoing] The answer you're looking for…

37:51.269 --> 37:53.771
a reason to be alive…

37:55.690 --> 37:57.233
[breathing shakily]

37:58.317 --> 38:00.319
Forget all of it, Arisu.

38:06.325 --> 38:08.035
[shivering] The-- the truth is

38:09.203 --> 38:11.122
everyone has a different answer.

38:13.874 --> 38:15.751
It doesn't matter now.

38:17.837 --> 38:19.171
You-- you don't need

38:20.131 --> 38:21.882
a-- a reason to live.

38:23.551 --> 38:24.969
[breathing heavily]

38:26.429 --> 38:29.432
This whole time
that we were looking for answers…

38:29.515 --> 38:31.100
[sobbing]

38:31.976 --> 38:34.228
…we've been searching side by side.

38:41.444 --> 38:43.404
That alone was all I needed.

38:45.239 --> 38:46.907
That was enough.

38:48.117 --> 38:50.119
[emotional music]

38:55.499 --> 38:58.711
You helped me realize what was important.

39:03.382 --> 39:04.842
It was you.

39:08.554 --> 39:10.306
It was you, Arisu.

39:21.484 --> 39:22.902
[gasping]

39:47.134 --> 39:49.303
[Mira] You poor thing.

39:55.768 --> 39:57.603
Looks like I've won.

40:05.861 --> 40:07.571
You'll be forfeiting now.

40:09.407 --> 40:11.075
Isn't that right, Arisu?

40:25.297 --> 40:27.383
And then… [gasps]

40:29.009 --> 40:30.970
…our game will be over.

40:34.306 --> 40:35.307
[chuckles]

41:17.600 --> 41:18.893
[Arisu] Usagi.

41:22.521 --> 41:24.482
[breathing shakily]

41:26.942 --> 41:28.068
Usagi…

41:30.196 --> 41:32.114
I want to feel your hand.

41:34.742 --> 41:36.368
Just one more time.

41:37.578 --> 41:39.580
[emotional music]

41:42.124 --> 41:43.918
Walk side by side.

41:45.503 --> 41:46.712
One more time.

41:53.052 --> 41:55.095
And I want to eat next to you.

42:01.644 --> 42:02.937
[Usagi] Me too.

42:15.074 --> 42:16.158
Tomorrow…

42:21.872 --> 42:23.082
I just want…

42:25.000 --> 42:27.836
to say good morning to you.

42:31.924 --> 42:34.218
I want to laugh with you every single day.

42:36.971 --> 42:38.264
And some day…

42:41.850 --> 42:44.311
I want us to climb a mountain.

42:46.272 --> 42:47.731
Just being with you…

42:49.984 --> 42:52.486
that's more than enough, Usagi.

42:55.531 --> 42:56.740
We may fight.

42:59.910 --> 43:02.496
But some days, that might be nice.

43:02.580 --> 43:03.706
[chuckles]

43:04.206 --> 43:05.291
[sniffles]

43:07.418 --> 43:08.877
I want you to live.

43:12.131 --> 43:13.549
I want that.

43:31.900 --> 43:33.902
I want to keep protecting you.

43:34.403 --> 43:36.405
[emotional music swells]

43:53.756 --> 43:54.923
Game on.

43:57.676 --> 43:58.802
Last round.

44:13.484 --> 44:15.486
[music fades]

44:29.541 --> 44:31.543
[wind whistling]

44:49.645 --> 44:51.897
- [Usagi] Arisu.
- [Arisu sighs]

44:53.190 --> 44:54.358
[Arisu] It's okay now.

45:07.496 --> 45:08.706
Here, take it.

45:20.259 --> 45:22.219
How beautiful that was.

45:28.392 --> 45:29.893
I do mean that.

45:36.525 --> 45:38.318
Let's finish off the game.

45:40.821 --> 45:42.489
Let's both do it for her.

45:45.743 --> 45:47.745
[gentle music]

46:15.689 --> 46:16.732
Yes!

46:31.914 --> 46:32.956
Okay.

46:39.505 --> 46:40.964
Yes!

46:58.565 --> 46:59.817
[sighs]

47:18.126 --> 47:19.503
Gah!

47:19.586 --> 47:20.546
[sighs]

47:24.258 --> 47:26.093
[laughing] Yes!

47:27.177 --> 47:29.096
Hmm! I win!

47:29.930 --> 47:30.889
[laughs]

47:34.101 --> 47:35.143
[giggles]

47:39.773 --> 47:41.775
[poignant music]

47:47.906 --> 47:49.074
Well done.

47:50.701 --> 47:52.619
You finished three sets.

47:54.246 --> 47:56.832
You didn't quit or forfeit the match.

48:01.253 --> 48:03.589
Congratulations, Arisu.

48:06.008 --> 48:08.594
[computer] The game has ended.

48:13.056 --> 48:14.099
Finally…

48:17.436 --> 48:18.687
Is it over?

48:26.403 --> 48:27.404
Yeah.

48:29.615 --> 48:31.033
We won, Usagi.

48:43.170 --> 48:44.463
[drops mallet]

48:48.675 --> 48:49.551
Well?

48:51.053 --> 48:53.722
What is this place? Can you tell me now?

48:58.977 --> 48:59.978
Arisu.

49:02.940 --> 49:04.608
You'll find out soon enough.

49:10.697 --> 49:12.616
You will be given two choices.

49:14.910 --> 49:16.495
No matter which one you pick,

49:18.038 --> 49:19.539
you will learn the answer.

49:22.084 --> 49:24.878
And you'll learn who you really are
when you choose.

49:26.838 --> 49:28.340
You'll soon find out.

49:31.677 --> 49:33.053
Life is just…

49:34.721 --> 49:36.431
a game we play together.

49:39.935 --> 49:41.645
You should try to enjoy it.

49:50.445 --> 49:51.571
[whirring]

50:02.916 --> 50:04.918
[emotional music swells]

50:12.300 --> 50:14.136
[computer] Congratulations.

50:14.761 --> 50:18.473
All of the games have now been cleared.

50:19.349 --> 50:21.351
[rumbling]

51:01.516 --> 51:03.393
[music fades and continues quietly]

51:29.544 --> 51:34.299
[computer] All surviving players
will be presented with two choices.

51:35.842 --> 51:38.095
Players must now all decide

51:38.178 --> 51:41.848
whether to accept
permanent residency in this country,

51:41.932 --> 51:43.850
or decline it.

51:45.102 --> 51:46.311
Once again,

51:47.270 --> 51:51.983
players must now decide
whether to accept permanent residency,

51:52.067 --> 51:53.735
or decline it.

51:55.403 --> 51:57.405
[fireworks continue exploding]

51:59.825 --> 52:01.034
I decline.

52:03.120 --> 52:04.913
[rustling]

52:04.996 --> 52:06.998
[whimpering]

52:14.673 --> 52:15.882
[gasps]

52:17.551 --> 52:19.094
[Aguni grunting]

52:20.846 --> 52:22.681
[Akane whimpering]

52:28.436 --> 52:30.188
[sobbing]

52:33.567 --> 52:34.609
And I…

52:36.153 --> 52:37.863
don't want it!

52:37.946 --> 52:39.698
[sobbing and gasping]

52:39.781 --> 52:41.783
[emotional music continues]

53:04.472 --> 53:05.807
I decline.

53:06.933 --> 53:08.685
[gasping]

53:21.239 --> 53:23.241
[rustling]

53:29.456 --> 53:31.249
[Kuina] Let's go back together.

53:44.346 --> 53:46.473
I accept, naturally.

53:47.766 --> 53:49.517
I will gladly take it as well.

53:57.359 --> 53:58.610
I want

54:00.195 --> 54:01.571
to turn it down,

54:02.155 --> 54:03.281
I think.

54:07.035 --> 54:08.578
What are you gonna say?

54:18.088 --> 54:19.798
I decline.

54:20.632 --> 54:22.801
[emotional music swells]

54:51.913 --> 54:53.081
I decline.

54:56.251 --> 54:58.169
I'm choosing not to stay here.

55:02.507 --> 55:03.675
Same for me.

55:07.929 --> 55:09.055
I don't want it.

55:22.444 --> 55:24.195
[music fades]

55:26.448 --> 55:27.866
[ice rattling]

55:27.949 --> 55:29.159
You want the usual?

55:31.911 --> 55:32.829
Sure, thanks.

55:34.414 --> 55:35.415
Here you go.

55:38.877 --> 55:39.711
Hey.

55:42.380 --> 55:43.214
What?

55:46.885 --> 55:48.470
One big-ass nose hair…

55:48.553 --> 55:49.929
Wait, what? [grunts]

55:50.013 --> 55:50.889
Really?

55:51.598 --> 55:54.100
- No.
- Aw, you're such a piece of shit!

55:54.184 --> 55:56.269
[both laughing]

55:59.856 --> 56:01.775
Ah, you just looked so depressed.

56:02.817 --> 56:06.780
Listen, did you know you can
pull out your nose hair with wax?

56:06.863 --> 56:09.449
- That would hurt so bad!
- And they never grow back?

56:09.532 --> 56:11.034
Nah, they still grow back!

56:11.117 --> 56:13.203
- Then using a trimmer is way better.
- Oh, sure.

56:13.286 --> 56:15.955
What if something
falls on top of you while you're doing it?

56:16.039 --> 56:19.626
- That would hurt even worse.
- Well, not as badly as an explosion.

56:19.709 --> 56:22.045
- Oh yeah?
- Yeah! [laughs]

56:22.128 --> 56:23.963
[Karube chuckles]

56:27.258 --> 56:28.301
I'm sorry.

56:30.178 --> 56:31.262
I'm sorry.

56:33.306 --> 56:34.599
It's my fault.

56:36.393 --> 56:37.227
I'm sorry.

56:38.561 --> 56:40.313
Oh, his fault, he says.

56:41.189 --> 56:43.066
Someone thinks highly of himself.

56:43.149 --> 56:47.362
I bet you think you're alive because
you're, like, a chosen one or something.

56:47.445 --> 56:50.323
I don't! It's thanks to you guys.

56:50.407 --> 56:55.245
Come on. That makes it sound like we all
sacrificed ourselves to keep you alive.

56:55.328 --> 56:58.415
Chota, hey. Wasn't that a little harsh?

56:58.498 --> 57:00.750
Arisu's missing
the whole point, seriously.

57:00.834 --> 57:01.918
[chuckles]

57:02.794 --> 57:03.878
What the hell?

57:04.921 --> 57:06.423
What are you trying to say?

57:07.924 --> 57:09.467
Just tell me, come on.

57:12.720 --> 57:14.264
Listen, man, it's like this.

57:16.474 --> 57:19.561
Across all these games,
there hasn't been a single one,

57:19.644 --> 57:21.646
not one, that you cleared on your own.

57:22.230 --> 57:24.566
You could go on thanking us
for the rest of your life

57:24.649 --> 57:26.359
and it still wouldn't be enough.

57:27.277 --> 57:28.236
Okay…

57:29.529 --> 57:31.990
Should I apologize
for the rest of my life, then?

57:34.367 --> 57:35.285
Don't be an idiot.

57:36.161 --> 57:38.037
We want you to live your life, man.

57:38.872 --> 57:40.707
Live it to the fuckin' fullest.

57:46.254 --> 57:47.255
All right.

57:49.048 --> 57:50.049
Promise.

58:00.935 --> 58:02.937
[chuckles softly]

58:08.943 --> 58:10.945
["Good Times" by Sam Medina playing]

58:12.614 --> 58:15.408
♪ Um, oh-um ♪

58:15.950 --> 58:17.702
♪ Good times ♪

58:17.785 --> 58:19.579
♪ It's all right ♪

58:19.662 --> 58:22.457
♪ So get ready to go ♪

58:23.082 --> 58:25.084
♪ It's such a good life ♪

58:25.585 --> 58:27.086
♪ Hot sound ♪

58:27.170 --> 58:30.798
♪ 'Cause now we're on the road ♪

58:30.882 --> 58:32.884
♪ Somethin' wrong ♪

58:33.510 --> 58:35.053
♪ Oh, sunny days… ♪

58:35.136 --> 58:37.722
[Chota] I'd be down with zombies
showing up in Shibuya.

58:37.805 --> 58:40.266
Everyone here gets bitten,
and they all turn into zombies.

58:40.350 --> 58:42.602
[Karube] Stop it with the zombie talk,
will ya?

58:42.685 --> 58:45.980
If zombies did show up here,
only Karube would survive.

58:46.064 --> 58:48.525
- You'd knock 'em out with one punch.
- [chuckles]

58:49.108 --> 58:51.569
I doubt that.
You'd be the one to survive, Arisu.

58:52.153 --> 58:53.446
Me? Why's that?

58:54.614 --> 58:55.949
'Cause I know you'd outsmart 'em.

58:57.534 --> 58:59.536
♪ The heat's turning on… ♪

58:59.619 --> 59:01.287
Shit. Let's do this.

59:01.371 --> 59:02.372
- Come on!
- Whoa--

59:02.455 --> 59:04.415
- Whoa!
- Whoa, what are you doing?

59:04.499 --> 59:06.960
You know, this is the first day
of your independence!

59:07.043 --> 59:09.128
- Coming through! Step aside!
- [Arisu] Whoa! Whoa!

59:09.212 --> 59:11.214
[Karube] Gangway!

59:11.297 --> 59:13.299
- ♪ It's all right… ♪
- Hey, slow down!

59:13.383 --> 59:15.677
♪ Get ready to go… ♪

59:16.594 --> 59:18.471
- [music fades]
- [rumbling]

59:19.597 --> 59:21.432
[muffled sounds]

59:47.125 --> 59:49.168
- [horn blares]
- Whoa! Whoa!

59:49.252 --> 59:50.920
- Get down!
- [engine revs]

59:51.004 --> 59:52.589
- Quick!
- [biker] You guys are crazy!

59:52.672 --> 59:54.549
- [horn blares]
- [all gasping]

59:55.508 --> 59:56.759
Okay, run! Run!

59:56.843 --> 59:58.761
- We can make it!
- Look, fireworks!

59:58.845 --> 59:59.887
- Run for your lives!
- Go!

59:59.971 --> 01:00:00.847
[horns blare]

01:00:00.930 --> 01:00:02.390
- [tires screech]
- Fuck, man!

01:00:02.473 --> 01:00:04.350
- [shrieking]
- Come on!

01:00:04.434 --> 01:00:06.394
[Arisu] Fuck, fuck! It's the police!
This is bad!

01:00:06.477 --> 01:00:08.396
- So bad! I'm sorry!
- [Karube] Oh no… Run!

01:00:08.479 --> 01:00:09.981
[all laughing]

01:00:11.024 --> 01:00:12.942
- [gates bleeping]
- [Arisu] The stairs!

01:00:14.944 --> 01:00:16.029
[sounds fade]

01:00:16.112 --> 01:00:17.905
[rumbling]

01:00:18.615 --> 01:00:19.866
[choral music]

01:01:00.823 --> 01:01:02.825
[sounds fade]

01:01:18.049 --> 01:01:20.051
[muffled rumbling]

01:01:43.408 --> 01:01:45.410
[muffled, distorted voice]

01:01:48.162 --> 01:01:49.497
[garbled radio chatter]

01:01:51.332 --> 01:01:53.084
[helicopter hovering overhead]

01:01:53.167 --> 01:01:55.586
- [man 1] Can you hear me? Sir!
- [siren wailing]

01:01:55.670 --> 01:01:57.463
- Can you hear me?
- [man 2] I need a check here!

01:01:57.547 --> 01:01:59.006
- [man 1] His vitals?
- [man 2] Now!

01:01:59.090 --> 01:02:00.216
[man 1] Copy that.

01:02:01.134 --> 01:02:02.218
We've got a pulse!

01:02:03.678 --> 01:02:04.762
He's breathing!

01:02:05.805 --> 01:02:07.432
He's alive! We need a stretcher!

01:02:08.015 --> 01:02:09.475
- Resume CPR.
- Okay.

01:02:10.101 --> 01:02:11.269
We need a gurney here!

01:02:11.352 --> 01:02:13.521
- Now! Hurry!
- [man 3 counting]

01:02:47.513 --> 01:02:50.808
[reporter 1] It has been two days since
a meteorite exploded over Tokyo…

01:02:50.892 --> 01:02:54.896
[reporter 2] Structural damage is
centered around a 10 km radius

01:02:54.979 --> 01:02:56.689
from Shibuya Park Street…

01:02:56.773 --> 01:02:58.024
[overlapping voices]

01:02:58.107 --> 01:03:02.862
[reporter 3] …has extended its condolences
to the following families.

01:03:02.945 --> 01:03:05.823
Some names are Kairi Nakamura,

01:03:06.491 --> 01:03:08.117
Daikichi Karube…

01:03:08.201 --> 01:03:09.660
[reporter 2] The government's set up…

01:03:09.744 --> 01:03:11.537
[reporter 3] …Kihiro Sato,

01:03:11.621 --> 01:03:13.748
Chota Segawa,

01:03:14.332 --> 01:03:16.167
Kodai Tatta,

01:03:16.250 --> 01:03:18.711
Saori Shibuki…

01:03:19.879 --> 01:03:22.131
Karube and Chota are dead now.

01:03:24.342 --> 01:03:25.676
And I get to live?

01:03:27.678 --> 01:03:28.971
Don't beat yourself up.

01:03:30.515 --> 01:03:31.891
It'll only make it worse.

01:03:35.686 --> 01:03:36.854
Survivor's guilt.

01:03:37.772 --> 01:03:39.607
It's a hell of a thing to deal with.

01:03:41.651 --> 01:03:43.861
"Why me? Why am I alive?"

01:03:45.071 --> 01:03:47.782
"Why couldn't they have been saved too?"
You know?

01:03:50.034 --> 01:03:52.829
Apparently, it happens
to most people after disasters.

01:03:53.704 --> 01:03:55.456
They end up blaming themselves.

01:03:59.335 --> 01:04:01.587
[sighs] But when they finally
found your body,

01:04:02.964 --> 01:04:04.757
your heart had completely stopped.

01:04:09.303 --> 01:04:10.721
A whole minute went by.

01:04:15.059 --> 01:04:18.437
Apparently, for a minute,
the borderlands had taken you.

01:04:21.148 --> 01:04:22.316
A minute?

01:04:23.234 --> 01:04:24.151
Yeah.

01:04:29.115 --> 01:04:30.783
[gentle music]

01:04:31.534 --> 01:04:32.827
A minute?

01:04:37.582 --> 01:04:38.624
You know…

01:04:40.835 --> 01:04:42.169
it felt like…

01:04:44.255 --> 01:04:45.590
a lot longer.

01:04:47.758 --> 01:04:50.595
Like I'd gone away for a long time.

01:04:57.518 --> 01:04:58.686
You know, uh…

01:04:59.979 --> 01:05:01.147
Dad cried. [chuckles]

01:05:03.316 --> 01:05:04.775
The last time he cried

01:05:06.110 --> 01:05:07.820
must've been when Mom died.

01:05:08.946 --> 01:05:09.864
[chuckles softly]

01:05:32.887 --> 01:05:34.931
[man coughing]

01:05:37.433 --> 01:05:39.435
[breathing heavily]

01:05:43.189 --> 01:05:44.774
What do you want?

01:05:47.401 --> 01:05:50.696
It looks to me like you must have
experienced a cardiac arrest.

01:05:51.948 --> 01:05:53.115
[scoffs]

01:05:53.199 --> 01:05:54.742
What are you, a doctor?

01:05:57.870 --> 01:05:59.246
Well, I did too.

01:06:01.040 --> 01:06:02.333
[sighs]

01:06:02.416 --> 01:06:03.626
What a coincidence.

01:06:07.088 --> 01:06:08.714
So we both almost died.

01:06:10.341 --> 01:06:11.842
You feel any different now?

01:06:13.302 --> 01:06:14.512
[sighs]

01:06:14.595 --> 01:06:15.513
I don't know.

01:06:16.806 --> 01:06:19.183
[sighs] I mean, I look a lot worse.

01:06:20.893 --> 01:06:21.852
What about you?

01:06:26.273 --> 01:06:28.818
I've been thinking a lot about my life.

01:06:30.236 --> 01:06:31.946
Choices I had to make.

01:06:32.697 --> 01:06:35.074
Pretty sure I'm gonna
be turning my life around.

01:06:36.283 --> 01:06:37.451
[Niragi scoffs]

01:06:37.952 --> 01:06:39.787
Or something like that.

01:06:40.579 --> 01:06:41.580
[sighs]

01:06:42.748 --> 01:06:45.042
You were a piece of shit, too, huh?

01:06:45.126 --> 01:06:46.460
You fucked up?

01:06:47.878 --> 01:06:48.838
I did.

01:06:49.338 --> 01:06:50.339
[laughs]

01:06:53.467 --> 01:06:54.677
[sighs]

01:07:06.313 --> 01:07:09.900
[man] Huh. After his cardiac arrest,
it's a miracle he's come this far already.

01:07:09.984 --> 01:07:12.528
- Could you get me some gauze, please?
- Yes, doctor.

01:07:19.869 --> 01:07:21.704
Is it someone you know?

01:07:21.787 --> 01:07:23.247
No. Not really.

01:07:28.419 --> 01:07:29.920
But I do understand.

01:07:30.963 --> 01:07:33.049
I bet he's trying to survive too.

01:07:34.341 --> 01:07:35.384
[nurse] He is.

01:07:56.072 --> 01:07:57.698
[man 1] Commencing cardiac massage.

01:07:57.782 --> 01:07:59.075
[man 2] Get the defib ready, now!

01:07:59.158 --> 01:08:02.078
- [woman 1] Right away, doctor!
- [man 3] Miss Ann, can you hear me?

01:08:02.161 --> 01:08:03.996
- Miss Ann!
- [man 2] Clear!

01:08:04.747 --> 01:08:06.248
- [thump]
- [man 4] Still no pulse!

01:08:06.332 --> 01:08:10.086
- [man 2] Again! Charge it!
- [woman 2] Yes, sir! Charge complete!

01:08:10.169 --> 01:08:11.629
- Clear! [grunts]
- [thump]

01:08:11.712 --> 01:08:12.963
[rapid bleeping]

01:08:13.047 --> 01:08:15.216
- [regular bleeping]
- We have a pulse!

01:08:15.299 --> 01:08:18.344
Normal sinus rhythm.
Heart rate is holding between 80 and 90.

01:08:18.427 --> 01:08:19.637
[man 2] She's back!

01:08:19.720 --> 01:08:21.013
Resume operation!

01:08:21.097 --> 01:08:22.807
- Forceps.
- [woman 1] Here, doctor.

01:08:33.192 --> 01:08:35.986
- Are you all right?
- [sighs] Yes.

01:08:36.487 --> 01:08:38.239
There's no need to rush at all.

01:08:38.322 --> 01:08:39.865
- You're doing very well.
- Okay.

01:08:56.507 --> 01:08:58.509
[breathing shakily]

01:09:05.641 --> 01:09:06.976
[gasps]

01:09:08.394 --> 01:09:09.645
[sobs]

01:09:12.940 --> 01:09:14.525
[mother crying]

01:09:16.944 --> 01:09:18.946
[emotional music]

01:09:28.122 --> 01:09:29.623
You came back to us.

01:09:51.228 --> 01:09:52.313
[father] Hikari.

01:10:03.908 --> 01:10:04.950
[gasps]

01:10:15.085 --> 01:10:18.756
[reporter] …has released two trillion yen
from the national treasury

01:10:18.839 --> 01:10:20.174
for emergency relief.

01:10:21.008 --> 01:10:25.012
A week has passed
since the meteorite exploded over Tokyo.

01:10:25.095 --> 01:10:30.601
Even now, all metro and railway operations
have been suspended in Tokyo,

01:10:30.684 --> 01:10:34.271
and many major roads
have been shut down as well.

01:11:11.850 --> 01:11:13.060
[Usagi] Sorry…

01:11:13.811 --> 01:11:15.562
Do you mind if I use it?

01:11:16.146 --> 01:11:18.190
Oh, I'm sorry. Go ahead.

01:11:45.676 --> 01:11:46.802
Hey, wait.

01:11:48.012 --> 01:11:49.013
Your change.

01:11:51.682 --> 01:11:52.516
[Usagi] Oh!

01:11:53.517 --> 01:11:54.643
Thanks a lot.

01:12:07.531 --> 01:12:08.449
Um…

01:12:09.158 --> 01:12:11.243
Sorry, but have we met before?

01:12:13.620 --> 01:12:14.872
I don't think so.

01:12:19.418 --> 01:12:20.461
Wait.

01:12:25.090 --> 01:12:27.259
Are you sure that I don't know you, miss?

01:12:28.510 --> 01:12:29.428
Uh…

01:12:33.640 --> 01:12:35.976
[chuckles] Are you, uh,

01:12:37.144 --> 01:12:38.479
flirting with me?

01:12:39.271 --> 01:12:40.731
Uh, no.

01:12:40.814 --> 01:12:42.107
It's not like that.

01:12:44.526 --> 01:12:46.779
Uh, wait. Wait. Stop!

01:12:47.446 --> 01:12:48.322
Um, miss.

01:12:48.989 --> 01:12:51.241
Would it be all right if I was?

01:12:51.325 --> 01:12:52.493
Flirting with you?

01:12:56.288 --> 01:12:57.456
[sighs]

01:13:01.710 --> 01:13:02.795
I'm sorry.

01:13:03.754 --> 01:13:05.130
That wasn't cool of me.

01:13:10.135 --> 01:13:13.389
[Usagi] I think maybe we have met before.

01:13:15.933 --> 01:13:17.851
Uh, was it last year?

01:13:18.644 --> 01:13:20.104
Or was it…

01:13:21.146 --> 01:13:22.398
When was that?

01:13:23.732 --> 01:13:25.776
[chuckles] I don't know.

01:13:27.069 --> 01:13:28.153
But we've met.

01:13:31.198 --> 01:13:32.574
[chuckles]

01:13:34.159 --> 01:13:35.285
[laughs]

01:13:38.205 --> 01:13:40.874
Uh, the sun's out. It's pretty nice.

01:13:42.626 --> 01:13:46.171
Do you want to maybe step out?
Go for a walk?

01:13:47.464 --> 01:13:49.007
Mm. Mm-hmm!

01:13:51.009 --> 01:13:53.011
[light, hopeful music]

01:14:14.116 --> 01:14:16.118
[music swells]

01:15:16.261 --> 01:15:17.846
[music fades]

01:15:29.191 --> 01:15:31.193
[ominous music]
